NASA Blue Marble day surface and Black Marble 2016 night lights

Day source:
https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/esd/eo/images/bmng/bmng-base/february/world.200402.3x5400x2700.jpg
NASA Earth Observatory Blue Marble: Next Generation February global base map,
based on Terra MODIS observations. Source size: 5400 x 2700.

Night source:
https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/esd/eo/images/imagerecords/144000/144897/BlackMarble_2016_3km_gray.jpg
NASA Earth Observatory image by Joshua Stevens, using Suomi NPP VIIRS data
from Miguel Roman, NASA Goddard Space Flight Center. Source size:
13500 x 6750.

The two bundled WebP files are Lanczos-resampled to a power-of-two
4096 x 2048 resolution and encoded at WebP quality 90. This preserves WebGL 1
longitude wrapping, materially improves close regional views, and avoids the
GPU-memory cost of decoding the non-power-of-two masters at runtime. The
browser blends both local textures at the astronomical day/night terminator;
it does not contact NASA at runtime.
